From a95bd2f8da7821bc899fcd1f1bcf4fe063896197 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gillinger <christian.gillinger@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:05:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] genesys: frame selection and magazine handling for the
 OpticFilm 135i

Four options, inactive on every other ASIC: 'frame' (which frame of the
loaded strip to scan, 1-6, the geometry being fixed by the holder),
'load-film' and 'eject-film' (the two-step magazine protocol -- the
operator reseats the magazine between the release and the next scan,
since SANE cannot prompt during sane_start), and a read-only 'magazine'
status line. sane_open/sane_close take the companion driver's process
lock around the device.
---
 backend/genesys/genesys.cpp | 285 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 backend/genesys/genesys.h   |   8 +
 2 files changed, 273 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

